;; The files of the round trip (bin/repr-c roundtrip; doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: C3b") that do not pass
;; every level, by corpus, each with its class (the classes below). Written by bin/repr-c roundtrip --record,
;; the classes kept. Read with the Clojure reader.
{:classes
 {:bad-specs-print "a declaration whose specifiers conflict (:c/bad-specs: long, short or int with _BitInt, the checker's \"both 'long' and '_BitInt'\") printed outside declare-specs as one normalized type: the reread loses the mark, level 1 differs (CS221 (b), CS232 (b), 2026-11-01: until a corpus file needs it; gcc-bitint's bitint-1.c does; deferred for v1, the user, 2026-11-03)"
  :cc-grammar "the reference accepts the file, the port's parser (cc's, C3's trees) does not: C23's attributes in positions cc's grammar lacks, the parenthesized storage-class compound literal, _Decimal64x, a declaration gcc's dialect takes (CS40 (a)'s rule; deferred to C4 and C7, CS80)"
  :converter-gap "a construct the converter does not write or writes losing a part: an octal _BitInt or d32 suffix, a function defined through a typedef or auto, __declspec, an empty literal's digits, an attribute list after a declarator's comma, nullptr as a case label's operand (CS83), C2y's if and switch declarations, read as a block that declares them and printed as that block (CS194 (a))"
  :eval-limits "the evaluated port's limits (CS60, CS78): a recursion deeper than the evaluator's 10,000 calls (a stack overflow), or a read past the round trip's budget (REPR_C_READ_BUDGET, 120 s; a third of it for the :full read's): deferred until C5 compiles repr/c"
  :macro-context "a recovered invocation or a printed expansion means another thing where the print stands: a name a later function-like macro takes (the original's tokens hidden from it), an invocation's stringized escapes and spacing (CS82)"
  :objects "the print is the same program (levels 1, 2, 4) but gcc -O0's object code differs: an asm label's section (CS81 (a))"
  :objects-macro-body "the print is the same program (levels 1, 2, 4) but gcc -O0's object code differs: the nop gcc places at a body's end whose closing brace stands on another line than its last statement, a body an invocation made that the print lays out on lines (CS81 (b), deferred)"
  :print-grammar "the :lines print holds what cc's grammar (the reread) or gcc refuses though the original did not: an attribute leading a type name, a recovered invocation of a pp-number with a UCN, a ref to #embed's resource the print's directory lacks (CS80)"
  :reexpansion "a macro invocation inside a larger one (not a whole node) is printed expanded, and a self-referential macro of the expansion (musl's #define stdout (stdout)) is expanded again by the reread: the forms gain the inner invocation's :c/macro (N6's limit; the objects equal)"
  :run-address "the original and the print run differently though their objects are equal: the program prints addresses (return-addr.c), a run's own nondeterminism"
  :self-include "the main file includes itself (#include __FILE__-like tests): its tokens are the main file's twice, refused by the converter"
  :split-declaration "a declaration begins in one file and ends in another (SPEC §4.3's split-declaration): refused"}
